			<div class="content" id="post-content-4832295">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre: Humerous Horror</p>
<p>Page Layout: A fairly standard SCP article layout with an interview log and an addendum at the end.</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch<br />
(The whole idea behind this is it's supposed to represent the dangers of gambling addiction)</p>
<ul>
<li>Its an anomalous coin that will reveal 3 different sides when flipped over. The 3rd side is anomalous.</li>
<li>When bet on and flipped, if the coin lands on the 3rd side it transforms whoever flipped it into a monster and then they kill and eat their opponent.</li>
<li>When someone has the coin it gives them a kinda high feeling (meant to be similar to the rush of gambling) that will continue as long as they continue to find victims to feed the monster. Thus they are encouraged to entice people into playing games and making bets on the coin. They tend to be more extroverted and friendly the longer they have it, learning how to swindle people in order to keep the feeling going. They're having fun but also hopelessly addicted to the power of the coin. (Note, the coin doesn't anomalously change the person's behavior, its not &quot;possessing&quot; them. It just makes them feel good, and they end up changing their behavior to chase the high.)</li>
</ul>
<p>Central Narrative: The foundation learns about a weird death in Las Vegas and finds a man named Mr. Exolia in police custody. He has this &quot;magic coin&quot; and the foundation wants it. But he hides it and won't reveal its location until the foundation agent agrees to make a bet with him on the flip of the coin. Exolia ends up losing the bet and agrees to come in willingly into foundation custody. The foundation can see Exolia knows a lot about this anomalous coin and try to get the knowledge out of him, but he toys with them, making a game out of it. Eventually a test is done where he gambles with a D-class and then transforms into the monster and kills the D-class. After this incident the coin is taken from him and he goes into withdraw symptoms. He's eventually given amnestics and released to witness protection. The coin is kept at a foundation site until it is stolen by a custodian.</p>
<p>Hook: Mr. Exolia's humorous yet dangerous nature. He is quick witted and funny, but also clearly is trying to trick people into making bets with him that could potentially get them killed.</p>
<p>Notes: This SCP is meant to symbolize the dangers associated with gambling addiction. The coin can bring great joy to one person (the person who has it), but terrible sorrow to another (the person who ends up killed by the monster).</p>

