<p>I haven't come up with its exact origin story yet, but I had a general idea that its very old and can adapt its non-anomolous sides to whatever currency is most prevalent in the time of each specific tale. So like in colonial times it could look like a shilling, in Europe it could look like a euro, in my first tale it looks like an American quarter. This is mostly just to keep it from being detected and to help it blend in no matter when or where someone has it.</p>
<p>The monster is an enlarged version of the person with the coin with 2 rows of sharp teeth, 5 spikes on its head in the shape of a crown (maybe the origin story could trace it back to some ancient king?). It would have redish skin and extra long arms that end in flesh and bone scythes that it uses to decapitate its victims. The transformation only lasts until the monster has finished off its victim(s), then they revert back to their normal human selves. I need to transfer the tale into my sandbox but then ill post a link for it.</p>
<p>Also, thanks for checking out my thread!</p>

