<p><em>noting that since there's a lot of stuff in the thread, I haven't read it all. I'm assuming the main post covers all the important details and apologies if I miss stuff as a result</em></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>The coins most interesting part isn't the monster but more so what it does to the people in possession of it. It makes them more exuberant, more fond of games and gambling, risk, chaos, but not necessarily evil.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>My concern here is that it feels a little too much like the coin is <em>forcing</em> this to happen; whereas a story like this often works best when the coin has some kinda property that gently encourages it and leads to people choosing to become this way. Like, imagine if the coin was anomalously lucky say, and caused people who gamble with it to win a bit more often than usual: not enough to be immediately obvious but enough to be beneficial; and in turn, this sense of always being able to win causes them to take more and more risks because they think it'll pay off and then eventually it doesn't, y'know?</p>
<p>This ties into a concern I have here: the monster feels irrelevant. Like, this has three faces, so presumably (though there's no indication of this) it has a 1-in-3 chance of landing monster side up; which in turn means they are very likely to have turned into a monster within 3 flips.</p>
<p>Beyond this my largest concern is: what story(s) are you actually telling here? Like you talk a lot about how this concept can be used to create stories and the general of like, how it affects someone who uses it but really what I want to know is the specific: what arc are you telling here? What are you putting in the SCP article and the tales?</p>
</div>
</div>
