<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I don't think the focus on 'Mr. Exolia' works for me here; particularly since it seems to rely entirely on him being humorous, which is super hard to pull off in text. In part it's also cos he doesn't really&#8230;do anything? He doesn't feel like a protagonist driving the story forward and in part that's because there's not really a story being driven forward? There's no-one here making choices that affect the outcome here and it feels&#8230;.lacking as a result?</p>
<p>There's also not really a sense of characters grow: they change somewhat throughout, but only when the story forces them to (e.g., the gambling and losing causes Exolia to become a monster, there's no personal transition from happy funny chill dude to anger because it's forced by the coin; then later he gets withdrawal symptoms but it feels unearned because he didn't <em>choose</em> to give up the coin).</p>
<p>The change of the transformation into a monster being implied to be non-permanent feels weird; though I'm still very unclear on what actually happens when someone is turned into a monster.</p>
